Linux sees everything as a file: regular files, directories, devices, and more.
🗂️ Access Control Lists (ACLs)
ACLs provide more fine‑grained permissions than the traditional rwx model and let you grant specific users or groups access to files or directories.
View ACLs: getfacl <path>
Add or change a user entry: setfacl -m u:<user>:<perm> <path>
Example: setfacl -m u:alice:rw test.txt
Add or change a group entry: setfacl -m g:<group>:<perm> <path>
Remove a user entry: setfacl -x u:<user> <path>
Remove all ACLs: setfacl -b <path>
