SED 
text editor like vi or nano.
sed is useful when you want to replace text or sentences in a large file.
Example:

sed -i 's/kramer/yare/g' seinfeld

Here, sed is the command. The -i flag stands for “in-place,” meaning it will replace the text permanently, and the previous text will be lost. The 's' stands for substitute, /kramer is the text to be replaced, and /yare is the new text. The g stands for global, meaning it will replace the text everywhere in the file. 
